  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "PeerSharp 3.0 is a major release with intentional breaking API changes: IClientEngine adds BEP 46 publishing/resolution and BEP 51 discovery members, and ITorrent.SetDownloadPathAsync now accepts a CancellationToken; consumers implementing or mocking these interfaces must update and recompile. New protocol support includes BEP 44 mutable/immutable DHT items with Ed25519 signatures, BEP 46 self-updating torrents, BEP 51 info-hash sampling and crawling, tracker enhancements from BEP 24/31/41, DHT read-only mode from BEP 43, upload-only signaling from BEP 21, and lt_donthave from BEP 54. Reliability and performance work covers parallel storage/session I/O, faster deterministic shutdown, cancellation and teardown races, rate limits on every peer transport, encrypted inbound uTP and MSE interoperability, pipelined-handshake preservation, metadata-request redundancy, tracker retry semantics, and extensive real-swarm, concurrency, trim, API-surface, and benchmark guards. Packages now include XML documentation and Source Link symbol packages.",
